But the showscore option affects version.feature_set, which is one of the
four magic numbers the game checks for deciding whether or not the save
file is compatible.
I suggest adding it to the IGNORED_FEATURES macro in util/makedefs.c.

A snippet from my makedefs.diff patch from
http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html :

-- cut here --
--- nh342off/util/makedefs.c	2003-08-30 03:08:16.000000000 +0300
+++ nh342jl/util/makedefs.c	2003-10-12 17:52:52.000000000 +0300
@@ -416,6 +416,9 @@
  * This should go away in the next version update.
  */
 #define IGNORED_FEATURES	( 0L \
+				| (1L << 17)	/* TEXTCOLOR */ \
+				| (1L << 20)	/* EXP_ON_BOTL */ \
+				| (1L << 21)	/* SCORE_ON_BOTL */ \
 				| (1L << 23)	/* TIMED_DELAY */ \
 				)
 
-- cut here --

This enables compiling SCORE_ON_BOTL, EXP_ON_BOTL and TEXTCOLOR in or out
without invalidating old bones, IF the struct sizes don't get changed
because of the number of bitfields making the structs go over some byte
limit.

